@prefix kb:     <urn:kbase:concept/> .
@prefix kpred:  <urn:kbase:predicate/> .
@prefix ktype:  <urn:kbase:type/> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

# ==============================================================================
# EXAMPLE WORKSPACE GRAPHS — tracked in git, copied into your workspace on setup
#
# THE BOUNDARY THIS FILE EXISTS TO MAKE OBVIOUS:
#
#   static/examples/*.ttl        TRACKED. Shipped with the app. Edit these and it
#                                is a code change, reviewed like any other.
#
#   reckons-workspace/kbs/**     IGNORED, entirely. This is YOUR graph data,
#                                written by the app's folder sync. Nothing here
#                                is ever committed, and that is deliberate: a
#                                personal notes graph and a grants pipeline are
#                                not source code and must not deploy with it.
#
# scripts/setup-reckons-workspace.sh COPIES these into the workspace if a graph
# of that name is absent. A copy, never a symlink — a symlink would make your
# first edit to a personal graph a modification of the repository, which is the
# exact confusion this separation exists to prevent.
# ==============================================================================

kb:example-workspace rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Example workspace graphs" ;
    kpred:description "Starter graphs demonstrating personal usage of Reckons.AI, separate from the project's own self-documenting graphs. Copied into reckons-workspace/kbs/ on setup, then yours to edit." ;
    kpred:principle "AN EXAMPLE THAT SHIPS IS AN EXAMPLE THAT IS TESTED. Until 2026-08-26 nothing under reckons-workspace/kbs/ was tracked at all — the .gitignore comment claimed 'the demo/starter fixtures already tracked under kbs/ stay tracked', and `git ls-files` returned zero. A fresh clone got an empty workspace and no worked example of what a personal graph looks like." ;
    kpred:principle "PERSONAL DATA IS NOT SOURCE. The separation is not a tidiness preference: production deploys from main on every push, so anything tracked is published. A personal notes graph in the repository is a personal notes graph on the internet." .
